  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cd79fd9f6a19c62ebc53ccd8cfd3ad754e6b333843bcd9b86f8fe3bcd5df6a2f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cd79fd9f6a19-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners distinguish between federal officers appointed to a second office and those who merely exercise additional duties within a single office."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cd79fd9f6a19c62ebc53ccd8cfd3ad754e6b333843bcd9b86f8fe3bcd5df6a2f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cd79fd9f6a19-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners contend that the four judges who began serving on the CMCR were appointed judges, which they say violates the dual\u2011office\u2011holding ban and disqualifies them from hearing the appeals."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cd79fd9f6a19c62ebc53ccd8cfd3ad754e6b333843bcd9b86f8fe3bcd5df6a2f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cd79fd9f6a19-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners note that Congress has sometimes expressly authorized military officers to hold a second, even civil, office, citing the CIA director as a common example."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cd79fd9f6a19c62ebc53ccd8cfd3ad754e6b333843bcd9b86f8fe3bcd5df6a2f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cd79fd9f6a19-0003-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 76,
                "start": 76
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argue that the Government\u2019s claim of rigorous administrative enforcement of the statute is empty."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Brian H. Fletcher (Respondent)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cd79fd9f6a19c62ebc53ccd8cfd3ad754e6b333843bcd9b86f8fe3bcd5df6a2f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cd79fd9f6a19-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 47,
                "start": 47
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Brian H. Fletcher (Respondent), according to Brian H. Fletcher (Respondent), the Government asserts that Section\u202f1259 gives this Court appellate jurisdiction to review decisions of the Court of Appeals for the Armed Forces."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cd79fd9f6a19c62ebc53ccd8cfd3ad754e6b333843bcd9b86f8fe3bcd5df6a2f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cd79fd9f6a19-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 70,
                "start": 70
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The Government maintains that the President merely ratified the placement of officers in the CMCR in a manner authorized by Congress."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "cd79fd9f6a19c62ebc53ccd8cfd3ad754e6b333843bcd9b86f8fe3bcd5df6a2f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-cd79fd9f6a19-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 71,
                "start": 71
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Government, the Government hopes the Court will hold that \u00a7\u202f973(b) does not prevent military officers from serving on the CMCR."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Government",
      "status": "complete",
